        <title>Distributary: my artwork proposal for Debian 14 &quot;forky&quot;</title>
        <published>2026-10-31T17:22:00+00:00</published>
        <updated>2026-10-31T17:22:00+00:00</updated>
        
        <author>
          <name>Samuel Henrique (samueloph)</name>
        </author>
        
        <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://samueloph.dev/blog/distributary-artwork-proposal-for-debian-14-forky/"/>
        <id>https://samueloph.dev/blog/distributary-artwork-proposal-for-debian-14-forky/</id>
        
        <content type="html" xml:base="https://samueloph.dev/blog/distributary-artwork-proposal-for-debian-14-forky/">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/&quot;&gt;&lt;img
src=&quot;https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/img/og.jpg&quot; width=&quot;1200&quot;
height=&quot;630&quot; alt=&quot;The Distributary wallpaper split on a diagonal: on the left,
the dark version, a gold river forking over dark green land with the Debian
logo; on the right, the light version, the same river as green ink on pale
paper&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In hydrology, a &lt;em&gt;distributary&lt;/em&gt; is a channel that forks away from a river and
flows on to the sea, the opposite of a tributary. Debian is the river much of
the Linux world forks from, so for a release called forky, that is my proposal
for its artwork: one river, many forks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All generated by code. A small Python program grows the river by the
rules of real deltas, and renders every wallpaper, login screen, boot splash
and GRUB background from it, dark and light, at any resolution: the showcase
offers 51 sizes to download, from phones to 8K.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/&quot;&gt;&lt;img
src=&quot;https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/img/colours.jpg&quot;
width=&quot;1728&quot; height=&quot;1208&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; alt=&quot;Distributary in its eight
colours, Forest, Violet, Midnight, Debian red, Rose on teal, Glacier, Lineage
and Silt, each as a dark and a light wallpaper side by side&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It comes in eight colours, and with the &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener external&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/editor/&quot;&gt;palette
editor&lt;/a&gt; you can fork
your own: change any colour or option live in your browser, or roll random
ones, then download the wallpaper or build the whole theme locally. Have a look
at the &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener external&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/&quot;&gt;showcase&lt;/a&gt; and at the
&lt;a rel=&quot;noopener external&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://wiki.debian.org/DebianArt/Themes/Distributary&quot;&gt;proposal on the Debian
wiki&lt;/a&gt;; the source is on
&lt;a rel=&quot;noopener external&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://salsa.debian.org/samueloph/distributary&quot;&gt;Salsa&lt;/a&gt; and
&lt;a rel=&quot;noopener external&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/samueloph/distributary&quot;&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
        
